  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1.69,
      "text": "Look down at your phone."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.69,
      "end": 4.5,
      "text": "It feels like magic, but inside,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.5,
      "end": 8.11,
      "text": "it is fundamentally just a handful of sand from the beach."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.11,
      "end": 11.78,
      "text": "Sand is made of tiny quartz crystals called silicon."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.78,
      "end": 16,
      "text": "Humans figured out that if you melt sand down"
    },
    {
      "start": 16,
      "end": 18.5,
      "text": "and carve billions of microscopic switches into it,"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.5,
      "end": 20.95,
      "text": "you can trap electricity inside."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.95,
      "end": 23.48,
      "text": "When a switch is OFF, it means ZERO."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.48,
      "end": 25.67,
      "text": "When it flips ON, it means ONE."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.67,
      "end": 27.5,
      "text": "That is all a computer is:"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.5,
      "end": 30.96,
      "text": "a beach of sand with lightning flipping switches."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.96,
      "end": 34,
      "text": "So how on earth did we teach sand to think?"
    }
  ],
